confirmed.fix:
**Fix:** list from one queue, sorted by the whole rank (tier, then the first flag's index, then name), with the lists in turn (pr, divergence, base) on a tie. That puts a seeded flagged collection's PR, divergence and base entries before any PR-own flagged entry.
- The change is about 3 lines: build `lists.flatMap((list, li) => list.todo.map(t => ({ list, li, ...t }))).sort((x, y) => byRank(x, y) || x.li - y.li)` and iterate it. The cut marker stays `stopped && list.done < list.todo.length`.
- **Checked in review-36e/fixes/fixcheck:**
  - users is listed in session.pr, session.divergence and session.base for s2 T=5, 20 and 45;
  - users is in boot.pr, boot.divergence and boot.base for `both 100 6`;
  - s1 200 delete 32 lists users in all three;
  - 235/235 data-capture, session, server and demo tests pass.

